Keep an ended call ended, and drop the registration of an offer that failed to send.

Origin: fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector, upstream meowcaller code (not from a pull request).

Why, two lifecycle defects on the 1:1 path:

- Call.setPhase accepted any transition, so a hangup that finished the call while the
  media loop was handling its first inbound audio packet could be undone: the loop set
  the phase back to Active and fired OnReady on a call that had ended. Ended is now
  terminal, setPhase reports whether it changed anything, and OnReady fires only when
  the move to Active happened.
- placeCall registers the call in e.calls before sending the <offer>, and returned the
  send error without unregistering it. The caller gets no Call to hang up, so every
  failed attempt left an entry, key material included, for the client's lifetime. It
  now finishes the call as "offer_failed" before returning.

Found in the review of fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector#387, round 14.

